<%# locals: (squads:, squads_address:, squads_app_url:, configured_upgrade_authority:, network:, vault:) %>
<%#
  (2b) THE PROGRAM UPGRADE AUTHORITY — a Squads V4 multisig, per cluster.

  READ, NOT QUOTED. Three places in this repo stated its membership and
  threshold and all three disagreed. `Solana::Squads` decodes the account.

  DERIVE THE VAULT PDA, NEVER COMPARE AGAINST THE MULTISIG ADDRESS. The account
  that sits in the program's upgrade-authority slot is a PDA OWNED BY the
  multisig — `[b"multisig", <multisig>, b"vault", 0]` under the Squads program.
  Comparing `solana program show`'s Authority line against the multisig address
  never matches, and reads as "the authority is wrong" when nothing is wrong.
  That mistake has been made twice here.
%>
<section class="card p-4 mb-6">
  <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-2 mb-1">
    <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-heading">Program upgrade authority (Squads multisig)</h2>
    <span class="font-mono text-2xs text-muted break-all"><%= squads_address %></span>
  </div>
  <p class="text-secondary text-sm mb-3">
    A <strong>different account entirely</strong> from the vault signer set
    above. It can redeploy the program; it cannot sign a vault action. Each
    cluster has its own, with its own membership.
  </p>

  <% if squads.nil? %>
    <p class="text-sm text-warning-ink mb-3">
      The Squads multisig could not be read on <%= network %>. Membership and
      threshold are unknown — do not substitute a number from a doc.
    </p>
  <% else %>
    <p class="text-sm mb-2">
      <span class="font-bold text-heading">
        Threshold <%= squads[:threshold] %> of <%= squads[:members].length %>
      </span>
      <span class="text-muted">
        (<%= pluralize(squads[:voting_members].length, "member") %> may vote)
      </span>
    </p>

    <ul class="space-y-1 mb-3">
      <% squads[:members].each do |member| %>
        <li class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-2 rounded-md border border-subtle bg-surface px-2 py-1">
          <span class="font-mono text-2xs text-heading break-all"><%= member[:address] %></span>
          <span class="text-3xs text-muted">
            mask <%= member[:mask] %>
            (<%= [("initiate" if member[:can_initiate]),
                  ("vote" if member[:can_vote]),
                  ("execute" if member[:can_execute])].compact.join(" · ").presence || "none" %>)
          </span>
          <% if vault && vault[:active_signers].include?(member[:address]) %>
            <span class="rounded bg-surface-alt px-1 py-px text-3xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-muted">
              Also a vault signer
            </span>
          <% end %>
        </li>
      <% end %>
    </ul>

    <dl class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-y-1 text-xs mb-3">
      <dt class="text-muted">Vault PDA index 0 (derived)</dt>
      <dd class="font-mono text-2xs text-heading break-all"><%= squads[:vault_pda] %></dd>
      <dt class="text-muted mt-1">What this app is configured to expect</dt>
      <dd class="font-mono text-2xs break-all <%= squads[:vault_pda] == configured_upgrade_authority ? "text-heading" : "text-danger-ink" %>">
        <%= configured_upgrade_authority %>
        <% if squads[:vault_pda] == configured_upgrade_authority %>
          <span class="text-3xs text-muted">— matches the derived PDA</span>
        <% else %>
          <span class="text-3xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wide">— does NOT match</span>
        <% end %>
      </dd>
    </dl>
  <% end %>

  <%# ── WHY THIS PAGE DOES NOT ACT ON SQUADS, AND WHAT A STOLEN KEY REACHES
      Recorded on the page rather than left implicit, because "we only handle
      the vault" reads as an omission unless the reasoning is visible.

      THE OVERLAP IS COMPUTED — NEVER CONCLUDED. This block used to end "but it is still below the threshold" with NO
      comparison to `squads[:threshold]`. It was true of the number in front of
      it on the day it was written (devnet overlap 2 against 3) and it is a
      CONCLUSION THE PAGE NEVER CHECKED.

      It inverts on the documented target. Both Squads are 3-of-5, and the
      intended five-member vault signer set IS the mainnet Squad's membership —
      so the overlap reaches 5 against a threshold of 3, and the page would
      reassure an operator that a holder of those keys "cannot execute here"
      while they could execute a PROGRAM UPGRADE. Understating blast radius, on
      the panel whose entire job is computing it.

      So the comparison is made, and each branch says only what its numbers
      support. Three states, because an unread vault set supports no claim about
      the overlap at all. %>
  <% members  = squads && squads[:members].map { |m| m[:address] } %>
  <% overlap  = (squads && vault) ? (members & vault[:active_signers]) : nil %>
  <% breached = overlap && squads && overlap.length >= squads[:threshold] %>

  <div class="rounded-lg border p-3 <%= breached ? "border-danger/40 bg-danger/10" : "border-subtle bg-surface-alt" %>">
    <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wide mb-1 <%= breached ? "text-danger-ink" : "text-muted" %>">
      <% if breached %>
        This console does not act on Squads — and right now that is a gap
      <% else %>
        Deliberately out of scope for this console
      <% end %>
    </p>
    <p class="text-xs text-secondary">
      <% if squads.nil? %>
        This Squad could not be read, so this page cannot say what a stolen key
        reaches here. Do not substitute a number from a doc.
      <% else %>
        This Squad needs <%= squads[:threshold] %> approvals out of
        <%= squads[:members].length %> members.
        <% if overlap.nil? %>
          The vault signer set could not be read, so this page cannot say how
          many seats the two authorities share — and therefore cannot say what a
          stolen vault key reaches here.
        <% elsif overlap.empty? %>
          No seat here is also in the vault signer set, so a stolen <em>vault</em>
          key reaches nothing on this authority.
        <% elsif breached %>
          <strong><%= pluralize(overlap.length, "seat") %> here
          <%= overlap.length == 1 ? "is" : "are" %> also in the vault signer
          set — at or above the threshold of <%= squads[:threshold] %>.</strong>
          A holder of those keys could <em>execute</em> a program upgrade, which
          is a strictly larger power than anything the vault signer set grants.
          Evicting them from the vault does not touch that: change this
          membership too, through the link below.
        <% else %>
          <%= pluralize(overlap.length, "seat") %> here
          <%= overlap.length == 1 ? "is" : "are" %> also in the vault signer
          set, which is the overlap worth watching —
          below the threshold of <%= squads[:threshold] %>, so a holder of those
          keys can create and vote on proposals and never carry one out.
        <% end %>
      <% end %>
      Squads already ships a web UI for changing membership, so this page links
      out rather than reimplementing a second, less-tested path to the same
      account.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-2 text-xs">
      <%= link_to "Open this cluster’s Squad on app.squads.so", squads_app_url,
                  target: "_blank", rel: "noopener",
                  class: "text-primary hover:text-primary-300 font-medium underline" %>
    </p>
    <p class="mt-1 text-3xs text-muted">
      That link serves the <strong><%= network %></strong> Squad — the cluster is
      carried by the ADDRESS in the URL, not by the host.
      <code>devnet.squads.so</code> is decommissioned, so there is no
      cluster-flavoured host to use instead; <code>app.squads.so</code> is the
      only surviving front end for both.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
